  (Q1) FORCE-PUSH DENY PATTERN — the permission glob matcher cannot carve `--force` out of `--force-with-lease` (string-prefix collision), so a `--force` deny risks blocking the safe `--force-with-lease` needed to update a rebased PR. Paths: (1) block `-f` only; (2) block `--force` broadly, accepting it also blocks `--force-with-lease` (recurring override friction); (3) drop force-push from the deny-list.
      CPO ANSWER: Path 1 — block only reckless `-f` (`git push -f` and `git push -f *`); leave `--force-with-lease`, long-form `--force`, and `git reset` allowed.
