      MLS, SPL, ED all landed at 5). Cheaper backfill, consistent with the current default.
    Path B: 10-11 seasons — matches the "Big 5 parity" tier (BL1/PL/PD/SA/L1), more history for
      trend metrics, materially bigger one-time backfill; these three aren't Big-5-tier leagues.
    RECOMMENDED: Path A (5 seasons) — the 10-11 season depth was a deliberate call for the Big-5
    parity tier specifically; nothing about these three argues for repeating it.
    CPO ANSWER: 5. (Path A, as recommended.)

  QUESTION 2 — the 6 women's leagues in #72's scope (NWSL, Frauen-Bundesliga, Serie A Women,
  Liga F, Première Ligue, FA WSL) plus Liga MX Femenil, all originally flagged "weak coverage
  (fixtures+standings only)" from the current-season-only check.
    RE-VERIFIED THREE TIMES IN-THREAD as the CPO pushed back on each round, each time with live
