  ⚠ VERDICTS: `analytics-engineer` PASS, `football-analytics-expert` PASS, `scope-auditor` **FAIL**.
  Both PASSing reviewers independently recomputed the counts from the files and reconciled them
  exactly (5 move / 34 stay / 39 total, 3 protected, 9 split on main → 7 on head, 2 fixed, **0 newly
  split**). The row-unit rule is sound. **What failed was a paragraph of prose I wrote about it.**

  ⛔ THE DEFECT: my `decisions_reserved` named four phrases and asserted that answering them "makes
  all 7 rows convertible". Wrong three ways, and checkable against the seed in one pass:
    (a) two of the seven — `finishing_efficiency_pct`, `finishing_efficiency_player_pct` — are
        blocked by **«on-target shots» inside their DESCRIPTION** ("not finishing the team's own
        on-target shots"), a phrase my list did not contain;
    (b) I said every block sits in the `interpretation`. It does not;
    (c) I listed **`deserved_points`, which is not split at all** — its `label_en` never carried the
        phrase, so nothing in that row disagrees with anything. It is HELD by the rule, which is a
        different thing from being BLOCKED, and I conflated the two.

  ⭐ THE RULE, and it is the census rule one level up: **A BLOCKER INVENTORY IS A CLAIM ABOUT THE
  FILE, SO IT MUST BE EXTRACTED FROM THE FILE.** I had already written "census with a pattern, not a
  list of spellings" into this very contract, then hand-listed the blockers from recall in the
  paragraph immediately below it. Derived, with site counts: «on-target shots» 4, «on-target threat»
  3, «on-target dominance» 1, «on target for − against» 1 — deciding the first three frees 6 of 7.

  ⛔⛔ FIFTH REGEX ERROR, AND THE FIRST FALSE POSITIVE — found only by chasing that FAIL. Widening
  the "on goal" detector to `on[ _-]?goal` (the fix for the fourth error) made it match the METRIC
  ID `shots_on_goal_difference_per_match`, which `deserved_points`' description quotes verbatim — so
  a fully consistent row read as SPLIT. Four errors from being too narrow, then one from being too
  wide, on the same phrase in the same file.

  ⭐⭐ THE RESOLUTION IS THE RULE STEP 4 ALREADY EARNED AND I DID NOT CARRY OVER: **ROLE, NOT
  PUNCTUATION.** Prose separates with a SPACE or a HYPHEN; an identifier separates with an
  UNDERSCORE. Row consistency is a claim about the ENGLISH A READER SEES, so an identifier must not
  count either way.

  ⭐ AND THE GENERAL FORM, which is the part worth keeping: **THREE DETECTORS, THREE JOBS, AND
  COLLAPSING ANY TWO OF THEM BROKE THIS SWEEP ONCE EACH.** (1) DECIDES what changes — strict.
  (2) COUNTS occurrences — maximally permissive, every separator; its only job is to miss nothing.
  (3) JUDGES reader-facing consistency — prose only, identifiers excluded. They are not
  interchangeable and the proof is measured: narrowing (2) to prose dropped the protected count from
