2026-09-02 CPO RULING — ROUND 5. A FOURTH INSTANCE, AND FOUR SWEEPS THAT FAILED FOUR DIFFERENT WAYS.

  ⭐ THE RULING, verbatim: **"round 5"**. A second round-cap override on the same MR.

  ⛔ WHAT WAS FOUND. `analytics-engineer-reviewer` FAILed round 4 — the round explicitly convened to
  close this class out — on a FOURTH stale statement in the same file, `10_home.md`: *"The Top
  players and Top teams blocks specified in §0 need six pieces of warehouse work, none of it
  built."* This MR ships two of those six. It sits in the prose sentence immediately BEFORE the
  "register is the authority" disclaimer, which by its own wording scopes to "this list" — the
  bullets that follow it — so no disclaimer reaches it.

  ⛔⛔ AND THE REASON IT SURVIVED IS THE WHOLE POINT: **THE PHRASE STRADDLES A LINE BREAK.** The file
  holds `none of it\nbuilt.` — so NO line-based grep can match it. Not my sweep, and not the
  reviewer's own quoted string either (`grep -ci "none of it built"` returns **0**).
  ⭐ **AND THAT TRAP IS WRITTEN IN `CLAUDE.md`, WHICH LOADS EVERY SESSION:** *"⚠ A line-based grep
  misses a phrase straddling a line break … Sweep whitespace-collapsed with comments stripped."*
  I had the rule in the always-loaded file and did not apply it.

  ⭐⭐ FOUR SWEEPS, FOUR DISTINCT FAILURE MODES, EVERY ONE A RULE I ALREADY HELD:
    1. searched the STRING changed ("9 count boards") rather than the CLAIMS falsified;
    2. searched only where a reviewer had already pointed, not the class;
    3. case-sensitive — "None of it is built" vs "none of it built";
    4. **line-based, so a phrase broken across two lines is invisible.**
  ⚠ Each fix addressed the previous mode and left the next one live. Widening a sweep one failure at
  a time IS the `fix_the_class_not_the_instance` failure, applied to sweeping itself.

  ⭐ THE METHOD THAT FINALLY WORKED, and the one to use from the start next time: **read each file
  whole, collapse ALL whitespace, match case-insensitively for the CLAIM in every phrasing including
  negations, then adjudicate every hit in writing.** Run on that basis it produced **38 hits across
  the tree**, of which exactly one was a genuine new defect and 37 were noise, struck text, other
  marts, or correctly-disclaimed list entries. A sweep is only trustworthy if it is allowed to
  return mostly noise; one that returns only the answer you expected has not searched.

  ⚠ COST, recorded because it is the honest measure: **three lines of SQL, five review rounds, and
  every FAIL was documentation drift rather than the change itself.**


